WEBVTT

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:01.629
Last video ended here.

00:00:02.071 --> 00:00:03.817
A used motorbike is bought with a twenty

00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:05.983
thousand dollar loan, at seven point two per

00:00:06.004 --> 00:00:07.769
cent a year, compounded monthly,

00:00:08.291 --> 00:00:09.936
repaid at four hundred dollars a month.

00:00:10.699 --> 00:00:12.866
A quick guess is twenty thousand divided by

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:14.995
four hundred, which is fifty repayments.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.401
But the first month's interest is a hundred

00:00:17.442 --> 00:00:19.805
and twenty dollars, so only two hundred and

00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:21.729
eighty dollars of that repayment pays off the

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:22.030
bike.

00:00:22.854 --> 00:00:25.184
Is it fifty repayments, about sixty,

00:00:25.728 --> 00:00:26.712
or more than seventy?

00:00:27.398 --> 00:00:27.864
Make a guess.

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:29.463
Here's the race.

00:00:30.169 --> 00:00:32.315
Without interest, the loan would be gone at

00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:32.837
fifty.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.076
With interest, it takes sixty.

00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:37.448
So how do we find that exactly?

00:00:38.272 --> 00:00:40.221
Start with what repaid means.

00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:43.474
After the last repayment, the balance is zero.

00:00:44.178 --> 00:00:45.485
And we already have a formula for the

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.194
balance after n repayments.

00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:50.658
A sub n equals P times one plus

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:53.220
r to the n, minus M times one

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:55.542
plus r to the n, minus one, all

00:00:55.663 --> 00:00:56.102
over r.

00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:58.848
Here P is twenty thousand,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.794
r is zero point zero zero six, and

00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:03.036
M is four hundred.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:05.446
So we set A sub n equal to

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:07.756
zero, and this time the unknown is n.

00:01:08.888 --> 00:01:11.397
Multiply both sides by r, and the first

00:01:11.458 --> 00:01:13.566
month's interest, one hundred and twenty dollars, appears.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.436
Gather the powers, and you get two hundred

00:01:16.457 --> 00:01:18.704
and eighty times one point zero zero six

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.711
to the n equals four hundred.

00:01:21.516 --> 00:01:23.464
So one point zero zero six to the

00:01:23.726 --> 00:01:25.353
n is ten sevenths.

00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:28.630
Take logs of both sides, and n comes

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:29.535
down from the power.

00:01:30.478 --> 00:01:33.043
n is log of ten sevenths over log

00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:35.828
one point zero zero six, about fifty-nine point

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:36.389
six two.

00:01:37.272 --> 00:01:39.178
This only works because four hundred is more

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:39.779
than the interest.

00:01:40.322 --> 00:01:42.291
If it only matched the interest, we'd divide

00:01:42.332 --> 00:01:44.481
by zero, and the balance would never change.

00:01:45.065 --> 00:01:46.753
If it were less, the right side would

00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:48.904
be negative, and no power could equal it.

00:01:49.616 --> 00:01:52.769
Fifty-nine point six two repayments isn't possible, so

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:53.592
which whole number?

00:01:54.397 --> 00:01:56.928
After fifty-nine repayments, there's still two hundred and

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:58.636
forty-eight dollars thirty-eight owing.

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:01.344
So the loan needs sixty repayments,

00:02:02.068 --> 00:02:04.072
and the last one is smaller, just two

00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:06.539
hundred and forty-nine dollars eighty-seven, once a month's

00:02:06.641 --> 00:02:07.342
interest is added.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.256
Always round the term up.

00:02:10.425 --> 00:02:13.366
The total actually paid is fifty-nine lots of

00:02:13.507 --> 00:02:16.327
four hundred, plus that last repayment, which is

00:02:16.548 --> 00:02:19.389
twenty-three thousand, eight hundred and forty-nine dollars eighty-seven

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:19.649
cents.

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:22.717
Take away the twenty thousand borrowed, and the

00:02:22.778 --> 00:02:25.426
bike cost three thousand, eight hundred and forty-nine

00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:27.252
dollars eighty-seven in interest.

00:02:27.962 --> 00:02:28.928
Now turn it around.

00:02:29.431 --> 00:02:30.958
Say you want the bike paid off in

00:02:31.138 --> 00:02:34.392
exactly four years, which is forty-eight repayments.

00:02:35.237 --> 00:02:36.489
What should each repayment be?

00:02:37.537 --> 00:02:40.351
Set A forty-eight equal to zero, and now

00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:41.656
M is the unknown.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.630
Add the repayment term to both sides, so

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.820
the loan's growth equals the repayments' growth.

00:02:47.503 --> 00:02:50.618
Then multiply both sides by r, and divide

00:02:50.679 --> 00:02:51.261
by the bracket.

00:02:52.085 --> 00:02:53.808
That gives M equals P

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.593
r times one plus r to the n,

00:02:57.175 --> 00:02:59.217
all over one plus r to the n,

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:00.119
minus one.

00:03:00.908 --> 00:03:03.194
Here P r is the same one hundred

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:03.655
and twenty,

00:03:04.218 --> 00:03:06.203
and one point zero zero six to the

00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:08.670
forty-eight is about one point three three.

00:03:09.573 --> 00:03:11.655
So M is one hundred and twenty times

00:03:11.697 --> 00:03:14.640
that power, over the power minus one, which

00:03:14.702 --> 00:03:17.125
is four hundred and eighty dollars seventy-eight cents,

00:03:17.386 --> 00:03:18.066
to the nearest cent.

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:21.097
That's about eighty dollars more each month.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.241
But forty-eight of them add to about twenty-three

00:03:24.322 --> 00:03:27.543
thousand and seventy-seven dollars, about seven hundred and

00:03:27.644 --> 00:03:29.384
seventy dollars less than before.

00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:32.199
The debt is gone sooner, so there's less

00:03:32.301 --> 00:03:33.125
interest altogether.

00:03:33.618 --> 00:03:34.164
One more question.

00:03:35.055 --> 00:03:37.124
At four hundred dollars a month, how much

00:03:37.205 --> 00:03:39.233
is still owed on the bike after two

00:03:39.314 --> 00:03:39.615
years?

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:42.990
That's after twenty-four repayments, so use the same

00:03:43.071 --> 00:03:45.219
formula with n equal to twenty-four.

00:03:46.062 --> 00:03:49.065
Twenty thousand times one point zero zero six

00:03:49.106 --> 00:03:51.668
to the twenty-four, minus four hundred times the

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:54.351
bracket, over zero point zero zero six,

00:03:54.853 --> 00:03:57.996
gives twelve thousand, seven hundred and ninety-five dollars

00:03:58.177 --> 00:03:58.897
twenty-six cents.

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:01.642
That's forty per cent of the time, but

00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:03.686
only about thirty-six per cent of the loan

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:06.391
is paid off, because the early repayments carried

00:04:06.432 --> 00:04:07.252
the most interest.

00:04:08.035 --> 00:04:09.982
Here's the idea behind three of the four

00:04:10.023 --> 00:04:10.704
calculations.

00:04:11.568 --> 00:04:14.393
Paid off means A sub n equals zero.

00:04:14.936 --> 00:04:16.724
Set it to zero, then solve for what's

00:04:16.766 --> 00:04:17.046
missing.

00:04:17.929 --> 00:04:20.292
For the amount still owing, just work out

00:04:20.313 --> 00:04:21.013
A sub n.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.116
Your turn.

00:04:24.839 --> 00:04:26.623
A loan of two hundred and fifty thousand

00:04:26.644 --> 00:04:28.768
dollars has interest at six per cent a

00:04:28.829 --> 00:04:30.472
year, compounded monthly.

00:04:31.134 --> 00:04:34.197
It's repaid in equal monthly repayments over twenty

00:04:34.258 --> 00:04:34.537
years.

00:04:35.299 --> 00:04:38.081
Find the monthly repayment, to the nearest cent,

00:04:38.502 --> 00:04:40.023
and the total amount paid.

00:04:40.686 --> 00:04:41.655
Pause here to answer.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:53.268
Here r

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.494
is half a per cent a month and

00:04:55.836 --> 00:04:57.299
n is two hundred and forty,

00:04:57.842 --> 00:05:00.087
so P r is one thousand two hundred

00:05:00.108 --> 00:05:00.588
and fifty.

00:05:01.191 --> 00:05:02.933
So M is one thousand two hundred and

00:05:03.054 --> 00:05:06.179
fifty, times one point zero zero five to

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.483
the two hundred and forty, over that power

00:05:08.544 --> 00:05:09.184
minus one.

00:05:09.966 --> 00:05:12.607
That's one thousand seven hundred and ninety-one dollars

00:05:12.928 --> 00:05:13.487
eight cents,

00:05:14.128 --> 00:05:16.289
and with two hundred and forty equal repayments,

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.050
the total paid is four hundred and twenty-nine

00:05:19.111 --> 00:05:21.712
thousand, eight hundred and fifty-nine dollars twenty.

00:05:22.553 --> 00:05:24.203
Two hundred and fifty thousand over two hundred

00:05:24.225 --> 00:05:25.553
and forty is wrong.

00:05:25.976 --> 00:05:27.884
It doesn't even cover the first month's interest.

00:05:29.631 --> 00:05:30.034
Last one.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.706
A loan of eighteen thousand dollars has interest

00:05:33.848 --> 00:05:36.494
at six per cent a year, compounded monthly.

00:05:37.179 --> 00:05:39.278
It's repaid at five hundred dollars a month.

00:05:39.962 --> 00:05:42.451
How many monthly repayments are needed to repay

00:05:42.492 --> 00:05:42.793
the loan?

00:05:43.518 --> 00:05:44.323
Pause here to answer.

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.895
The first month's interest is ninety dollars,

00:05:57.536 --> 00:05:57.735
so

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.317
one point zero zero five to the n

00:06:00.799 --> 00:06:03.060
is five hundred over four hundred and ten,

00:06:03.361 --> 00:06:05.221
which is fifty over forty-one.

00:06:05.983 --> 00:06:06.745
Taking logs,

00:06:07.327 --> 00:06:09.694
n is about thirty-nine point seven nine.

00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:12.444
Round up, so it's forty repayments.

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:14.215
Thirty-nine is wrong.

00:06:14.981 --> 00:06:17.748
After thirty-nine repayments, there's still about three hundred

00:06:17.769 --> 00:06:19.112
and ninety-three dollars owing.

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:23.408
So one formula answers all four questions:

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.710
set the balance to zero for three of

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.452
them, and just work it out for the

00:06:27.493 --> 00:06:28.292
amount still owing.

00:06:29.035 --> 00:06:30.352
Now turn the money around.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:33.698
Instead of borrowing, you save towards your first

00:06:33.739 --> 00:06:34.159
apartment:

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.401
two hundred dollars at the end of every

00:06:36.442 --> 00:06:38.563
month, in an account that earns interest.

00:06:39.248 --> 00:06:40.902
How much will you have after five years?

00:06:43.668 --> 00:06:44.470
Here are the key notes.

00:06:45.114 --> 00:06:46.841
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:46.903 --> 00:06:47.384
to copy them.
